# SBOM (generated, not committed) / SBOM (生成物、コミット対象外)
# FIND-WAVE4-V4-FINAL-SEC-L-03 (Wave 4 V4): SBOM artifacts are intentionally gitignored
# and must be regenerated on demand via `pnpm sbom` (CycloneDX 1.6). The lockfile
# (`pnpm-lock.yaml`) is the single source of truth for the production dependency tree;
# any stale entry observed in a locally-cached `sbom.cdx.json` (e.g. an outdated
# `hono@4.12.16` row after a `4.12.18` bump in `package.json` `pnpm.overrides`) is
# acceptable because (i) the artifact is not committed, (ii) CI / release flows
# regenerate the SBOM from the current lockfile state, and (iii) EU CRA Art.13(8)/14(2)
# transparency is fulfilled by SBOM-on-demand semantics, not by tracked artifacts.
sbom.cdx.json
sbom.cdx.xml

